spans.s:
--rice balls given on ceremonial occasions to पितृस्: three to be given; like the calf in search of the cow lost in the stall, मन्त्र takes them to the पितृस्; to be given in the name of the gotra of the person;
1: Br. III. २०. १०-16.
can be given to cows, Brahmanas, females, crows, hen or thrown into fire or water; the middle पिण्ड can be eaten by the wife which leads to increase of सन्तानम्;
2: M. १६. २१, ३५, ५३-54; वा. ७१. १०; ७५. २५, ३६.
पिण्डदानम् on the १२थ् day after death is supposed to be the पाथेयम् or food for the way to heaven;
3: M. १७. ४६. ५५.
seven पिण्डस् for seven generations;
4: Ib. १८. 5 and २९.
giving of, in the तीर्थस् of the नर्मदा;
5: Ib. १८६. १५. ३९; २३९. ३४.
at गया with tila.
6: वा. १०५, १२, ३३; १०८. १५, २१; ११०. २३-59.

--city of: its sages visited द्वारका;
1: भा. X. ९०. २८[3].
the sages who knew of कृष्ण's advent to वैकुण्ठ left for this place;
2: Ib.
